# Backend API base URL (no trailing slash, no /api/v1 suffix)
# Local `npm run dev` ignores this and proxies /api to http://localhost:8000,
# so a phone on the same Wi-Fi can open http://<laptop-ip>:5173.
# Production:  https://your-backend.onrender.com  (or whatever your deployed backend URL is)
# If a phone calls the API host directly (not through the Vite proxy), add that
# page origin to the backend FRONTEND_URL list.
VITE_API_BASE_URL="http://localhost:8000"
